# ♿ Accessibility

## Core Rules
- WCAG 2.1 Level AA minimum
- Test: keyboard-only, screen readers, axe DevTools
- Semantic HTML first, ARIA only when needed

## HTML & Elements
- Use `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation
- Semantic: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`
- Never `<div>` or `<span>` when semantic elements exist

## Keyboard
- All interactive elements keyboard accessible
- Visible focus states required
- Logical tab order, no traps
- Support Esc (close modals), Arrow keys (lists)

## ARIA
- `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` for elements without visible text
- `aria-describedby` for context
- `aria-live` for dynamic updates
- `role` only when semantic HTML insufficient

## Forms
- Pair `<label htmlFor>` with all inputs
- Visible labels (not just placeholders)
- Error messages via `aria-describedby`
- `aria-required="true"` for required fields
- Group with `<fieldset>` + `<legend>`

## Color & Contrast
- Normal text: 4.5:1 minimum
- Large text (18px+/14px+ bold): 3:1
- Never rely on color alone
- Support light/dark modes with proper contrast

## Media
- Images: meaningful `alt` text (decorative: `alt=""`)
- Videos: captions + transcripts
- Audio: transcripts

## Checklist
- [ ] Keyboard navigable with visible focus
- [ ] Semantic HTML, ARIA where needed  
- [ ] Alt text on images
- [ ] Labels on forms, proper contrast
- [ ] Tested with screen reader + axe DevTools
